-/*
- * This header contains various key-related definitions and helper functio=
n.
- * UBIFS allows several key schemes, so we access key fields only via thes=
e
- * helpers. At the moment only one key scheme is supported.
- *
- * Simple key scheme
- * ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
- *
- * Keys are 64-bits long. First 32-bits are inode number (parent inode num=
ber
- * in case of direntry key). Next 3 bits are node type. The last 29 bits a=
re
- * 4KiB offset in case of inode node, and direntry hash in case of a diren=
try
- * node. We use "r5" hash borrowed from reiserfs.
- */
